research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.proof-contracts.json:7096:          "quote": "1. $\\mathbb{Q}_{\\mathbb{R}}$ is dense in $\\mathbb{R}$, that is, $\\overline{\\mathbb{Q}_{\\mathbb{R}}} = \\mathbb{R}$ ([[def-limit-point-r]]); 2. $X$ is dense in $\\mathbb{R}$; 3. every nonempty open subset of $\\mathbb{R}$ is uncountable ([[def-countable]]). Claim 2 is not a symmetry of claim 1: the rationals are dense because they are *constructed* to approximate, whereas the irrationals are dense because there are too many points in any interval for a countable set to exhaust it, which is why claim 3 is proved alongside and used for it.",
